From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:34:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06912/11362] [outer-loop] bp35: round-9 move confirmed safe,
 switch 3 reached (still null)

Round-9 gpt-5.6-sol session confirmed round 8's flagged 50/50: stepping
RIGHT from (7,21) to (8,21) is SAFE. Made major further progress from
there -- sealing row-13 X hazards creates a traversable ceiling, and
even reopening one is safe in a controlled transition (another
correction to earlier assumptions). Reached and clicked switch 3 for
the first time this game, reversing gravity. The downward return dies
entering column 2 (a real hazard, confirmed independent of the
228-action timer -- died at action 210).

The session proposed a "corrected" column-3 descent but could not
execute it live (budget exhausted). The outer loop independently
tested both: the first 209 actions replay cleanly to level=5 matching
the report, but the full 221-action sequence INCLUDING the proposed
fix also dies (GAME_OVER, level=0). The proposed fix does not work
either -- confirmed via direct replay, not assumed. No new level
banked; frontier stays at level 5. Next attempt should not retry this
exact substitution; the real safe descent from (3,12) remains unsolved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
